#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186310907 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e970fe-cff8-50e3-9b94-67ad97b03da7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Power of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76b87126-f2aa-53d9-8621-d47ca3e6d8b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310909} {:answer/id #uuid "0aeb5094-770f-5ce2-8bcf-f308652e7de4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 & 24 \\\\ -24 & -8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310910} {:answer/id #uuid "b7d4a1f2-ac0e-59e1-a0cb-e750ba37fda6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 24\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310911} {:answer/id #uuid "4f845142-dd21-541c-8588-0d3cbe9ded3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310912} {:answer/id #uuid "95e3a20e-43e8-5a74-8e64-ecd1654323c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310913}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0aeb5094-770f-5ce2-8bcf-f308652e7de4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 & 24 \\\\ -24 & -8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310910} :answer-field/id #uuid "8921c2ef-bb2d-5a86-bdca-59c3bf7347ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310908}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a0990577-78da-5706-a148-fc38d54b37ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-130582" :question/problem "If $U=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]$, then ${U}^{3}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, to find ${U}^{2},$ we multiply $U$ by itself:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{U}^{2} & =U\\cdot U \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${U}^{3}={U}^{2}\\cdot U,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{U}^{3} & ={U}^{2}\\cdot U \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & 24 \\\\ -24 & -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186310914 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "61443225-bc08-5d36-a603-3a1d7e392a98" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Matrix Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2fda9c8-7ae1-583d-b5b0-3f8105d5c35a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -6 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310916} {:answer/id #uuid "bc48d304-5608-59c0-bf0f-212e59aadf15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310917} {:answer/id #uuid "c83e22f8-b3de-5a66-95b9-bd18ffb596c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310918} {:answer/id #uuid "56453ca0-b56d-5a07-8753-b14af48c034c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310919} {:answer/id #uuid "2e646f1d-ceb6-5b3c-b5f0-781f2f09a1e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310920}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c83e22f8-b3de-5a66-95b9-bd18ffb596c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310918} :answer-field/id #uuid "55b49f2f-315e-50d2-ab17-0103385b9d24" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310915}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c5573f21-e824-5c9e-8e76-3403856afb46" :question/math-academy-id "q-130684" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $D=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -6 & -4\\end{aligned}].$  Find $f(D)$ if $f(X)={X}^{2}-4.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & ={X}^{2}-4 \\\\  & ={X}^{2}-4I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(D)={D}^{2}-4I.$ \n\nLet's calculate ${D}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}^{2} & =D\\cdot D \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -6 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -6 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(D):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(D) & ={D}^{2}-4I \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]-4[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4-4 & 0+0 \\\\ 0+0 & 4-4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186310921 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "61443225-bc08-5d36-a603-3a1d7e392a98" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Matrix Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7571ea9-2826-5359-b120-3769ff804141" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310923} {:answer/id #uuid "198b4223-2a24-5ab5-8230-0222934b6ea6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310924} {:answer/id #uuid "e84f2c60-6a6d-508b-b60d-0a9965461e17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310925} {:answer/id #uuid "bf08239f-1d68-5160-ad5b-0e1fb6f3d9c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310926} {:answer/id #uuid "a841a8ed-ad3e-5b11-ade8-a0f28fe88f75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310927}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a841a8ed-ad3e-5b11-ade8-a0f28fe88f75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310927} :answer-field/id #uuid "d245895a-81d2-5c09-98e5-29d373f826a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310922}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6097bb1d-9d7a-56b4-9d4d-09d460a9e165" :question/math-academy-id "q-130687" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].$ Find $f(C)$ if $f(X)={X}^{2}-X+5.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & ={X}^{2}-X+5 \\\\  & ={X}^{2}-X+5I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(C)={C}^{2}-C+5I.$\n\nLet's calculate ${C}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{2} & =C\\cdot C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(C):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(C) & ={C}^{2}-C+5I \\\\  & =C-C+5I \\\\  & =5I \\\\  & =5[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186310928 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e970fe-cff8-50e3-9b94-67ad97b03da7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Power of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fae2432a-ab72-5165-b137-f96496ceb78f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310930}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fae2432a-ab72-5165-b137-f96496ceb78f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310930} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c443ab1-9612-5cee-b897-aa9fa3b1616d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310929} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e4b4630b-c1bb-58d4-a36d-ebe7355b517b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310932}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4b4630b-c1bb-58d4-a36d-ebe7355b517b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310932} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ccbd69a-3b3a-500d-b3d9-6d1ef6e28f9a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310931} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db725281-85e6-5318-9e46-7f6546de1ecc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310934}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db725281-85e6-5318-9e46-7f6546de1ecc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310934} :answer-field/id #uuid "75586b69-c552-5ed2-b7a4-65dfad170694" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310933} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf56bec0-e03c-57e2-9971-a623f57127ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310936}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf56bec0-e03c-57e2-9971-a623f57127ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310936} :answer-field/id #uuid "9661c867-4dbd-5792-b10d-7d5b0925d509" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310935}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7d702ccd-7591-5326-bec7-9db4775aa0ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-279430" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $F=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find ${F}^{3}.$\n\n| ${F}^{3}=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, to find ${F}^{2},$ we multiply $F$ by itself:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{2} & =F\\cdot F \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${F}^{3}={F}^{2}\\cdot F,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{3} & ={F}^{2}\\cdot F \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 36 \\\\ 18 & 9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186310937 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "61443225-bc08-5d36-a603-3a1d7e392a98" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Matrix Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23dc6ba8-fc36-5bfd-9021-9c961c7e7a75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}14 & -15 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310939} {:answer/id #uuid "6c078ef4-8c14-5c6e-bc27-5afbd6518004" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 12 \\\\ -11 & 17\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310940} {:answer/id #uuid "ffa4e7e2-243a-5796-882a-4a9c4e1bac36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}17 & -12 \\\\ -2 & 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310941} {:answer/id #uuid "9e7c4629-6014-5bb2-ae08-1b36afba66e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}17 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310942} {:answer/id #uuid "bc2e7b22-3711-5518-8f5e-b61b6bc4ab3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}22 & -8 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310943}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ffa4e7e2-243a-5796-882a-4a9c4e1bac36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}17 & -12 \\\\ -2 & 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310941} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9ef4e72-d2b8-538f-bd92-a4068a60ecdb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310938}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "84dd1552-3f60-57dc-aae2-e0aaa6ebc5f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-32321" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].$ Find $f(A)$ if $f(X)={X}^{2}-3X+1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & ={X}^{2}-3X+1 \\\\  & ={X}^{2}-3X+I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(A)={A}^{2}-3A+I.$\n\nLet's calculate ${A}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 15\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(A):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(A) & ={A}^{2}-3A+I \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 15\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 15\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 18 \\\\ 3 & 9\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10-(-6)+1 & 6-18 \\\\ 1-3 & 15-9+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}17 & -12 \\\\ -2 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
